1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,050
Have you heard of these dance moves?
你听说过这些舞蹈动作吗？

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:04,900
The lego leg?
乐高腿？

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,040
A clock blender?
时钟搅拌机？

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,650
Helicopter?
直升机？

5
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:10,390
Don't worry.
别担心。

6
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:14,850
By the end of the summer, you may know all these words!
到夏天结束时，你可能就会知道所有这些词了！

7
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:23,770
Paris is preparing to host the Olympic and Paralympic games, and a new sport will be making its debut.
巴黎正在准备主办奥运会和残奥会，一项新的运动将首次亮相。

8
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:28,220
Breaking is also known as breakdancing.
Breaking也被称为霹雳舞。

9
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:44,290
The dance sport is characterised by stylised footwork, acrobatic movements and freezing, where the B-boy or B-girl stops all movement, often upside down and balancing on one hand.
这项舞蹈运动的特点是风格化的脚步动作、杂技动作和定格，即霹雳舞男孩或女孩停止所有动作，常常是倒立并用一只手保持平衡。

10
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:53,990
From power moves like windmills and head spins, breakdancers really push the limits of physicality and creativity.
从风车和头转等力量动作来看，霹雳舞者真正突破了体能和创造力的极限。

11
00:00:53,990 --> 00:01:05,900
It was in the streets of the Bronx, New York, in the 1970s that breaking emerged as a revolutionary dance form, deeply rooted in hip-hop culture.
霹雳舞于20世纪70年代在纽约布朗克斯区的街头兴起，成为一种深植于嘻哈文化的颠覆性的舞蹈形式。

12
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:10,250
It's come a long way from there to the world stage in Paris.
从那里到巴黎的世界舞台，它走过了漫长的道路。

13
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:33,660
Athletes from around the world will showcase their skills in one-on-one battles, where each dancer has 60 seconds to impress the judges with their improvisation and proficiency in six criteria: creativity, versatility, performance skills, personality, technique and musicality.
来自世界各地的运动员将在一对一的对决中展示他们的技能，每位舞者有60秒的时间，通过在创造力、多样性、表演技巧、个性、技术和音乐性这六个标准的即兴表演和水准来打动评委。

14
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:44,650
However, as breaking moves from a lifestyle to a competitive sport, some fear it risks losing its spontaneity and creativity.
然而，随着霹雳舞从一种生活方式转变为竞技体育，一些人担心它可能会失去自然性和创造力。

15
00:01:44,650 --> 00:02:11,830
Thorsten Sufke, President of the Berlin Dance Sport Association, emphasises that breaking is an expression of urban culture, representing the raw energy of the streets, while B-Boy Carl Ferdinand Beccard expresses concerns that the Olympic format may suppress the artistic freedom of breaking, reducing it to a checklist of predefined moves.
柏林舞蹈运动协会主席托尔斯滕·苏夫克强调，霹雳舞是城市文化的一种表达，代表着街头原始的能量，而霹雳舞者卡尔·费迪南德·贝卡德则表达了对奥运赛制可能压制霹雳舞艺术自由、将其简化为一份预定动作清单的担忧。

16
00:02:11,830 --> 00:02:21,210
Whichever way you look at it, you can expect thrilling dance performances never before seen at an Olympics this summer.
无论你怎么看，你都可以期待今年夏天在奥运会上看到前所未有的激动人心的舞蹈表演。
